; The PRIMARY conformance world for the ImperialRent BSL port train (Material
; Base @9.0, Checkpoint A campaign; plan
; `docs/superpowers/plans/2026-08-18-imperialrent-port.md`; frozen source:
; `src/babylon/engine/systems/economic.py::ImperialRentSystem`, `step()` at
; `:46-86`). World 1 of 12 — all four IMPLEMENTED phases (Extraction, Tribute,
; Wages, Decision; Phase 4/Subsidy is Director-RESERVED, Constitution IX.5,
; plan §6, and does not land), the NO_CHANGE non-binding control (plan §9's
; per-world seed matrix, row "1 primary").
;
; **Task 1 scope.** This file is the scenario ceremony ONLY — no
; `imperial-rent/*` rule pack content yet (that is Task 2 onward). It exists
; to (a) prove the scenario loads clean against the newly-registered
; "imperial-rent" system via a load-smoke probe, (b) carry the frozen-mirror
; provenance for `imperial_rent_conformance.py`, and (c) host THE SPIKE
; (Step 5) that proves the seven content-unprecedented query/write shapes
; §3/§8 of the plan need — the throwaway spike rules ran in temporary Rust
; tests, verified green, then deleted; verdict recorded at the bottom of this
; header. Later tasks in this train grow `content/rules/imperial-rent.bsl`
; against this SAME scenario, chosen as the world where every phase produces
; a non-trivial (but non-crisis) result — declaration order is NodeId order;
; do not renumber when extending.
;
; **Enum order is a hash-bearing transcription of the frozen Python
; declaration order (ADR195)** — do not reorder:
;   `src/babylon/models/enums/social.py:34-41` — SocialRole (CORE_BOURGEOISIE
;   PERIPHERY_PROLETARIAT LABOR_ARISTOCRACY PETTY_BOURGEOISIE
;   LUMPENPROLETARIAT COMPRADOR_BOURGEOISIE INTERNAL_PROLETARIAT
;   CARCERAL_ENFORCER).
;
; **`social-class/active` is `int intensive`, not `extensive`** — corrected
; against `consciousness-ternary-conformance.bscn:227` (a 0/1 latch is a
; per-node state, never a summed quantity; the plan's own §8 field table
; names this as a deliberate correction against the earlier draft, which had
; claimed `extensive` while asserting verbatim reuse). No `bool` type token
; exists on the live `.bscn` deffield dialect (`scenario.rs::load_deffield`).
;
; **B7 STRUCK (Task 0 dossier CORRECTIONS item 1, Step 3): no
; `social-class/class-consciousness` field is minted.** The frozen
; `class_consciousness_from_node` accessor (`kernel/node_access.py:15-37`)
; already ports to the ALREADY-DECLARED `social-class/revolutionary` field —
; `solidarity.bsl:18-24` performs the identical re-point for the same
; accessor, and ADR211 records it independently. `periphery-worker`'s
; `revolutionary 0.2p` below is what the plan's own table called
; "class-consciousness 0.2" — same value, corrected field name.
;
; **`social-class/wages-paid`/`value-produced` are redeclared `real
; extensive` here** (B5, D191) — `consciousness-ternary-conformance.bscn`
; declares them `int extensive`; Task 0 Step 4(f) settled that a `real
; extensive` redeclaration is legal and the `:default -1` sentinel idiom
; (unused in THIS file — no rule reads them yet) continues to typecheck
; regardless, since no load/typecheck path compares a binding default's
; literal kind against its field's declared type. Neither field is SEEDED on
; any node below — no rule in this task's scope reads or writes them (the
; "no defaults" contract requires seeding only what a NON-OPTIONAL binding
; reads; both are write-only targets of `r06`, landing Task 5), matching the
; dossier's Step 3 clarification: absence is legal, only a required binding
; over an absent field is fatal.
;
; **`social-class/effective-wealth`/`unearned-increment`/`ppp-multiplier`
; are declared but not seeded** for the same reason — all three are
; write-only targets of `r06` (Task 5); no binding in this train's Task 1-4
; scope reads them.
;
; **The carrier — field-guarded, not constant-scored (D198, plan §3.1).** One
; `NodeType/INSTITUTION` node, `imperial-rent-register`, carrying the
; `rent-`-prefixed roster PLUS B8's two unprefixed latch fields
; (`institution/superwage-crisis-known`/`-tick`, declared under
; `decomposition.bsl`'s own names — the cross-pack seam, plan §2.1/D194).
; `institution/rent-carrier` is seeded `1` here — the D198 discriminator that
; lets `(select-max (nodes NodeType/INSTITUTION) (field-of it
; institution/rent-carrier))` resolve THIS node even in a world that also
; loads `decomposition.bsl`'s `carceral-register` (a lower-id INSTITUTION
; node under a naive constant-score tiebreak). This world mints only ONE
; INSTITUTION node, so the discriminator and a constant-score `select-max`
; agree by construction here; THE SPIKE Step 5(f) proves the discriminator
; resolves correctly even when a SECOND, lower-id, zero-carrier INSTITUTION
; node is present — a permanent test, own inline fixture (not this file).
;
; **`institution/rent-wages-outflow` is NOT declared (D199)** — the frozen
; `tick_context["wages_outflow"]` is a per-tick local `_save_economy` never
; persists; declaring it would fabricate hash-bearing state the frozen
; engine does not have. See plan §3.1's own reasoning.
;
; **Three seeding facts, corrected against the earlier plan draft (Task 0
; dossier, discharging the plan's own self-correction in §9):**
;   1. `institution/rent-repression-level` is seeded `0.5`, not `0.3` — it
;      matches `defines.survival.default_repression` (`defines.yaml:167`),
;      the frozen `_load_economy` fallback's own default, so the explicit
;      seed and the fallback can never describe two different worlds.
;   2. `institution/rent-wages-outflow` is not declared at all (above).
;   3. The seeding law is NOT "every declared field on every node" — see
;      the wages-paid/value-produced/effective-wealth paragraphs above.
;
; Five social classes, one carrier (declaration order fixes NodeId — never
; renumber when extending):
;
;   core-bourgeoisie    CORE_BOURGEOISIE, active, wealth 10000 — the
;                       EXPLOITATION target, the TRIBUTE recipient, the
;                       WAGES payer. Three roles, one node, matching the
;                       frozen circuit's own topology (Amin/Wallerstein).
;   periphery-worker    PERIPHERY_PROLETARIAT, active, wealth 500,
;                       revolutionary 0.2p (B7's re-point target) — the
;                       EXPLOITATION source; non-zero consciousness makes
;                       the frozen `rent = eff * wealth * (1 - consciousness)`
;                       factor provable (a zero consciousness would make the
;                       `(1 - c)` term structurally invisible, 1.0 always).
;   comprador           COMPRADOR_BOURGEOISIE, active, wealth 800 — the
;                       TRIBUTE source; non-zero wealth makes the frozen
;                       `source.wealth = cut_amount` OVERWRITE (not `sub`)
;                       provable — a zero-wealth comprador can't distinguish
;                       `set` from `sub` (both would leave 0).
;   labor-aristocracy   LABOR_ARISTOCRACY, active, wealth 300,
;                       production-value 40 (SEEDED — the frozen
;                       `la_production` dict's per-node reformulation,
;                       `production.py:194`) — the WAGES target.
;   petty-b             PETTY_BOURGEOISIE, active, wealth 250 — the
;                       non-participant witness: no edge touches it, and
;                       EVERY field of it must stay unchanged post-tick.
;   imperial-rent-register  INSTITUTION — the carrier (above).
;
; Edges: EXPLOITATION (periphery-worker -> core-bourgeoisie), TRIBUTE
; (comprador -> core-bourgeoisie), WAGES (core-bourgeoisie ->
; labor-aristocracy) — matching the frozen engine's own edge topology
; exactly (`economic.py`'s three `query_edges` loops). Each edge's
; `<namespace>/value-flow` is seeded `0` via `(edge-attr ...)` (D156) — the
; per-tick recorded flow, written fresh every tick a later rule runs
; (`graph.update_edge(..., value_flow=...)` in every one of the three
; frozen phases). Structural `strength` is a bare `1` — a presence marker
; only, matching `production-conformance.bscn`'s own convention; nothing in
; this pack reads edge strength.
;
; **§8's 23 `defconst`s, all at shipped values** (`src/babylon/data/
; defines.yaml:71-99,374`). Mint no new coefficient. Two are POSITIVE
; transcriptions of a frozen NEGATIVE value (`austerity-wage-delta`,
; `crisis-wage-delta`) — Task 0 Step 4(a) settled that no BSL literal syntax
; spells a negative fractional number in ANY position (every suffixed kind's
; lexer arm refuses negativity unconditionally); the sign is applied at the
; r08 use site (Task 7) via `sub`/the landed `(- 0 x)` idiom, not here.
; `economy/initial-rent-pool` is a bare `Int` literal (`100`, not `100.0$`
; or `100.0r`) deliberately: `institution/rent-pool` is declared `real`
; (Task 0 Step 4(d)), and `Int / Real` (or `Real / Int`) both fall through
; `apply_arith`'s `_ => real_lane` promotion cleanly — a `Currency`-typed
; denominator would instead hit `apply_arith`'s unconditional
; `(Value::Currency(_), other) => Err(E-TYPE-030)` arm for a `Real`
; numerator, and a `Ratio`-typed one is a THIRD runtime variant `real_lane`
; never promotes either; bare `Int` is the only spelling that avoids both
; traps for r08's pool-ratio division (Task 6/7 scope, verified here so
; Task 1 does not leave a landmine for it).
;
; **THE SPIKE VERDICT (Step 5, recorded here per the plan's own
; instruction).** Two throwaway spike rules were run through the real
; `run_once_into` driver — one against this exact scenario (proving (a)
; through (e) and (g)), one against a small inline two-INSTITUTION-node
; fixture built only inside the test file (proving (f), since this
; scenario mints exactly one INSTITUTION node by design) — then deleted
; (their bodies never landed in this file or in `content/rules/`):
;   (a) `(for-each (neighbors self EdgeType/EXPLOITATION :out
;       NodeType/SOCIAL_CLASS) ...)` fires for `periphery-worker` (the sole
;       EXPLOITATION source) and is empty (D127 hash-neutral) for every
;       other class — LOADED AND EVALUATED CLEAN.
;   (b) `(update-edge (edge-between EdgeType/EXPLOITATION self it)
;       exploitation/value-flow (set 1))` writes the `.bscn`-seeded
;       `exploitation/value-flow` edge attribute — LOADED AND EVALUATED
;       CLEAN, the write observed on the post-tick edge.
;   (c) the same `for-each` body issued BOTH `(update-node self ...)` and
;       `(update-node it ...)` — both writes observed.
;   (d) a nested `(guard <pred> <effect> <effect> <effect>)` with THREE
;       effects (one `emit`, two `update-node`) LOADED AND RAN, all three
;       firing together when the guard's predicate held.
;   (e) `(field-of it social-class/role)` compared by `=` against
;       `SocialRole/CORE_BOURGEOISIE` inside that same guard — typechecked
;       and evaluated correctly (true for `core-bourgeoisie`, the sole
;       EXPLOITATION target in this world).
;   (f) `(select-max (nodes NodeType/INSTITUTION) (field-of it
;       institution/rent-carrier))` resolved the REAL carrier
;       (`rent-carrier 1`) over a lower-id decoy INSTITUTION node
;       (`rent-carrier 0`) — proving the discriminator, not ascending-id
;       tiebreak, decides the winner. LOADED AND EVALUATED CLEAN; kept as a
;       PERMANENT test (not deleted with the rest of the spike).
;   (g) a `for-each` over `(nodes NodeType/SOCIAL_CLASS)` (5 elements)
;       issuing a repeated, `it`-independent `(update-node self ... (set
;       42))` alongside a repeated `(add 1)` on a different field — the
;       `set` writes landed as "last write wins" (the value observed after
;       the tick is exactly 42, not accumulated or refused), and the `add`
;       writes DID accumulate (5x, not 1x) — confirming Task 0 Step 4(e)'s
;       static reading of `structural_verbs.rs` against the real driver,
;       exactly as predicted, no refusal, no surprise.
; No shape refused. Full command/output evidence:
; `imperial_rent_conformance.rs`'s own module doc comment and the Task 1
; report.
(scenario imperial-rent/conformance
  (defvocabulary NodeType (SOCIAL_CLASS INSTITUTION))
  (defvocabulary EdgeType (EXPLOITATION TRIBUTE WAGES))
  (defenum SocialRole (CORE_BOURGEOISIE PERIPHERY_PROLETARIAT LABOR_ARISTOCRACY PETTY_BOURGEOISIE LUMPENPROLETARIAT COMPRADOR_BOURGEOISIE INTERNAL_PROLETARIAT CARCERAL_ENFORCER))

  (deffield social-class/role enum SocialRole)
  (deffield social-class/active int intensive)
  (deffield social-class/wealth real extensive)
  (deffield social-class/production-value real extensive)
  (deffield social-class/revolutionary probability intensive)
  (deffield social-class/wages-paid real extensive)
  (deffield social-class/value-produced real extensive)
  (deffield social-class/effective-wealth real extensive)
  (deffield social-class/unearned-increment real extensive)
  (deffield social-class/ppp-multiplier coefficient intensive)

  (deffield institution/rent-carrier int extensive)
  (deffield institution/rent-pool real extensive)
  (deffield institution/rent-tribute-inflow real extensive)
  (deffield institution/rent-wage-rate coefficient intensive)
  (deffield institution/rent-repression-level intensity intensive)
  (deffield institution/rent-aggregate-tension coefficient intensive)
  (deffield institution/superwage-crisis-known int extensive)
  (deffield institution/superwage-crisis-tick int extensive)

  (deffield exploitation/value-flow real intensive)
  (deffield tribute/value-flow real intensive)
  (deffield wages/value-flow real intensive)

  ; EconomyDefines/TimescaleDefines, src/babylon/data/defines.yaml:71-99,374.
  ; `austerity-wage-delta`/`crisis-wage-delta` are POSITIVE transcriptions of
  ; a frozen NEGATIVE value (Task 0 Step 4(a) — no fractional literal spells
  ; negative in any position); the sign applies at r08's use site (Task 7).
  (defconst economy/extraction-efficiency 0.8c)
  (defconst economy/comprador-cut 0.9c)
  (defconst economy/super-wage-rate 0.2c)
  ; `superwage-multiplier`'s declared domain is >= 0.0 (unbounded above);
  ; 1.0 sits exactly at the coefficient boundary [0,1] — legal today,
  ; fragile under modding (production-conformance.bscn's own
  ; `base-labor-power-annual 1.0c` precedent, same caveat).
  (defconst economy/superwage-multiplier 1.0c)
  (defconst economy/superwage-ppp-impact 0.5c)
  ; Bare Int, not a `$`/`r`-suffixed literal — see the header note above
  ; (Task 0 Step 4(d), the r08 pool-ratio division).
  (defconst economy/initial-rent-pool 100)
  (defconst economy/pool-high-threshold 0.7c)
  (defconst economy/pool-low-threshold 0.3c)
  (defconst economy/pool-critical-threshold 0.1c)
  (defconst economy/min-wage-rate 0.05c)
  (defconst economy/max-wage-rate 0.35c)
  (defconst economy/negligible-rent 0.01c)
  (defconst economy/trpf-coefficient 0.0005c)
  (defconst economy/rent-pool-decay 0.002c)
  (defconst economy/bribery-wage-delta 0.05c)
  (defconst economy/austerity-wage-delta 0.05c)
  (defconst economy/iron-fist-repression-delta 0.1c)
  (defconst economy/crisis-wage-delta 0.15c)
  (defconst economy/crisis-repression-delta 0.2c)
  (defconst economy/bribery-tension-threshold 0.7c)
  (defconst economy/iron-fist-tension-threshold 0.5c)
  (defconst economy/trpf-efficiency-floor 0.1c)
  (defconst timescale/weeks-per-year 52)

  (node core-bourgeoisie NodeType/SOCIAL_CLASS
    (social-class/role SocialRole/CORE_BOURGEOISIE)
    (social-class/active 1)
    (social-class/wealth 10000)
    (social-class/production-value 0)
    (social-class/revolutionary 0.0p))

  (node periphery-worker NodeType/SOCIAL_CLASS
    (social-class/role SocialRole/PERIPHERY_PROLETARIAT)
    (social-class/active 1)
    (social-class/wealth 500)
    (social-class/production-value 0)
    (social-class/revolutionary 0.2p))

  (node comprador NodeType/SOCIAL_CLASS
    (social-class/role SocialRole/COMPRADOR_BOURGEOISIE)
    (social-class/active 1)
    (social-class/wealth 800)
    (social-class/production-value 0)
    (social-class/revolutionary 0.0p))

  (node labor-aristocracy NodeType/SOCIAL_CLASS
    (social-class/role SocialRole/LABOR_ARISTOCRACY)
    (social-class/active 1)
    (social-class/wealth 300)
    (social-class/production-value 40)
    (social-class/revolutionary 0.0p))

  (node petty-b NodeType/SOCIAL_CLASS
    (social-class/role SocialRole/PETTY_BOURGEOISIE)
    (social-class/active 1)
    (social-class/wealth 250)
    (social-class/production-value 0)
    (social-class/revolutionary 0.0p))

  (node imperial-rent-register NodeType/INSTITUTION
    (institution/rent-carrier 1)
    (institution/rent-pool 100)
    (institution/rent-tribute-inflow 0)
    (institution/rent-wage-rate 0.2c)
    (institution/rent-repression-level 0.5i)
    (institution/rent-aggregate-tension 0.0c)
    (institution/superwage-crisis-known 0)
    (institution/superwage-crisis-tick 0))

  (edge EdgeType/EXPLOITATION periphery-worker core-bourgeoisie 1)
  (edge-attr EdgeType/EXPLOITATION periphery-worker core-bourgeoisie exploitation/value-flow 0)
  (edge EdgeType/TRIBUTE comprador core-bourgeoisie 1)
  (edge-attr EdgeType/TRIBUTE comprador core-bourgeoisie tribute/value-flow 0)
  (edge EdgeType/WAGES core-bourgeoisie labor-aristocracy 1)
  (edge-attr EdgeType/WAGES core-bourgeoisie labor-aristocracy wages/value-flow 0))
